 // Core numbering is the Snapdragon 888's: 0-3 A55, 4-6 A78, 7 X1. Each worker is pinned to one cpu of its set and checked
 // with sched_getcpu() at both ends (cpu_ok = workers that stayed). Each P2 / X1 / X2 cell runs 1 s of warm-up, then 2 s
 // measured. On a host without Linux affinity the sets are only thread counts (cpu_ok=-1).
+// 0002-d-rows (memo-05 §4 D2, D3): every block starts with "hdr" lines (lmk properties, zram, PSI, meminfo, vm; an
+// unreadable source gives e<errno>). Block "p2" ends with D2's "p2d" rows (K1 at TR 128 and Y1b against stock on one
+// pinned A78, hot and cold, plus Y1b on a kept-row list); block "p2d" runs D2 alone, block "hdr" only the header.
